ist customer organisations, their users and addresses, serving warehouse, minimum shelf-life requirement, orders and order lines. An order must have one or more lines, each for at least one pack, a saved address belonging to that organisation, a delivery date permitted by its warehouse calendar and cut-off, and a choice of partial delivery or delivery complete. A duplicate submission of the same order does not create a second order. Invalid dates, addresses, quantities or cross-organisation requests are refused without creating or changing the order."},{"kind":"data","text":"On submission, allocate only Released stock from the serving warehouse, never above available quantity, using earliest expiry first and skipping lots that fail the customer’s minimum remaining shelf life on the requested delivery date; equal-expiry lots with more stability budget used are chosen first. Lines can be split across lots. Complete-only orders reserve no stock unless all lines can be fulfilled; partial orders retain available allocations and back-order the balance. Back orders are filled automatically in submission order when suitable stock is released. Dispatcher overrides require a reason and cannot bypass the Released or shelf-life rules. Concurrent submissions cannot allocate the same stock twice."},{"kind":"permission","text":"Persist order status and per-line allocated and outstanding quantities. Customers can change or cancel their own order before packing; cancellation returns allocations to availability. After packing, customer changes and cancellation are refused; a dispatcher may cancel and receives the applicable allocation-restoration result. When allocated stock becomes On Hold, Rejected, Recalled or Expired, remove that allocation, attempt replacement allocation, and make the outcome visible to the dispatcher."},{"kind":"data","text":"Persist warehouse stock quantities and allocation state so available, allocated and quarantined quantities can be viewed by product, lot 